{
  "_comment": "Sony DualShock 4 over Bluetooth: input report 0x11 (in hidraw read() — up to 78 bytes). The useful data is the same as in the USB report 0x01, but shifted by +2 bytes (hid-sony/hid-playstation read them from rd+2). Verified on samples of a real report (sticks 80 7f 80 7f at bytes 3–6). Mode 0x11 is enabled by the kernel's system driver; if the device sends only short 0x01 reports, the driver is not loaded. There is no rumble here: the BT output needs a 0x11 report with a CRC32, which is not implemented yet.",
  "name": "Sony DualShock 4 (Bluetooth, report 0x11)",
